{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the generations of Aaron and Moses.</b> That is, the priests and the Levites. And it counts the sons of Aaron first, separately, as it is written: ״ויבדל אהרן להקדישו״. But the sons of Moses were not separated from the Levites, and therefore their generations are included among the Levites who descended from Amram." "<b>On the day that YHWH spoke to Moses.</b> That is, on that day Aaron had four sons, but afterwards Nadab and Abihu died, as is explained there. Rabbi Yochanan said: ״לפני ה' מתו נדב ואביהוא״ — this teaches that the death of the sons of the righteous is difficult before the Holy One, blessed be He, when they die in his lifetime."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:54.535545581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}